        &lt;description&gt;Create an independent identification rule for the Windows Server CI class, using the Asset Tag attribute as the highest-priority identifier. Use the CI Class Manager to configure this rule (use the Replace button) -&amp;gt; take note that previously inherited identification rules will no longer be used - recreate those which you will still need and add the new one afterwards.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
Good to know: normally servers are identified by the serial number or the serial number + other attribute, but our Windows Server class has the best data quality for asset tags, so we want to modify identifiers to reflect this to improve data quality.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
Simulate the update of the a Windows Server CI using Identification Simulation feature.&amp;#13;
&amp;#13;
Bonus point:&amp;#13;
Commit the change you saw during simulation to CMDB using IRE API through the background script&amp;#13;
